{"_comment": "HAND-WRITTEN oracle truth table. Every row below was derived by reading the advisory's range events against the OSV spec — `introduced` opens INCLUSIVE ('0' = -inf), `fixed` closes EXCLUSIVE [introduced, fixed), `last_affected` closes INCLUSIVE [introduced, last_affected], sibling ranges OR together — and NOT by executing depguard.oracle. That independence is the whole point: the eval gate recomputes gold with the same functions the tools call, so a sign flip inside record_containment moves prediction and label together and CI stays green at correctness 1.0000 (verified: inverting the `fixed` bound to inclusive flips 13 of 29 golden verdicts, including the lodash 4.17.21 headline case, while correctness stays 1.0000). This table is the independent check. Rows are weighted toward boundaries, because a boundary is where a sign flip shows.", "_schema": {"advisory_id": "str", "ecosystem": "str", "name": "str", "version": "str", "expected_contained": "bool", "human_rationale": "str"}}
